      "writtenOn": "2026-06-10T14:45:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Although the term `meaningful` is not explicitly seen in the decoder, it is not a non-standard syntax element. It represents the encoder-side decision logic for the standard AV1 syntax element `mode_ref_delta_update`.\n \nReverting the CL would fix the bug but take away the optimization (~0.01% BD-Rate gain). We feel that it is good to keep this optimization and fix the issue. Please check the result of reverting the optimization CL.\n\nOptimization done in [CL98781](https://aomedia-review.googlesource.com/c/aom/+/98781):\nPrior to this CL, the encoder signaled the `mode_ref_delta_update` bit unconditionally. This forced it to redundantly write 0 (\"unchanged\") in the bitstream for every single mode_ref_delta element (8 refs + 2 mode), even if nothing had changed from the previous frame.\nThe CL optimized this by adding a look-ahead check. If none of the delta values have changed, the encoder sets `meaningful` to 0 (signaling `mode_ref_delta_update \u003d 0`). This completely bypasses the need to write the `changed` bit for every element, yielding a ~0.01% BD-Rate improvement.\nDuring this optimization, the author removed the surrounding `if (lf-\u003emode_ref_delta_enabled)` guard, which introduced the current signaling bug.\n\n```\n                     Instruction Count    \n                         Reduction(%)                     BD-Rate Loss(%)\ncpu   Resolution      Encoder    Decoder       avg.psnr    ssim      vmaf    vmaf_neg  uvq_1p5\n 1      LOWRES2        0.008      0.038         0.0099    0.0002   -0.0003    0.0070   0.0000\n\n 6      LOWRES2        0.007     -0.012         0.0019    0.0018   -0.0243   -0.0084   0.0000\n 6      MIDRES2        0.002      0.006         0.0057    0.0008    0.0107    0.0099   0.0000\n 6      Average        0.005     -0.003         0.0038    0.0013   -0.0068    0.0007   0.0000\n```",
